  "nl_text": "This schema is for a database that stores information about a community of users who can ask and answer questions, known as Stack Overflow. The schema includes eight tables, each representing a different type of data.\nThe first table, \"badges,\" stores information about the badges that users can earn for their contributions to the community. Each row in this table represents a single badge, and it includes columns for the badge's ID, the user who earned it, the name of the badge, and the date it was earned.\nThe second table, \"comments,\" stores information about the comments that users can leave on questions and answers. Each row in this table represents a single comment, and it includes columns for the comment's ID, the post it is attached to, the score of the comment, the text of the comment, the date it was created, the user who created it, and the user's display name.\nThe third table, \"postHistory,\" stores information about the history of a post, including when it was created, when it was last edited, and who edited it. Each row in this table represents a single revision of a post, and it includes columns for the revision's ID, the type of revision, the post it is attached to, the revision's GUID, the date it was created, the user who made the revision, and the text of the revision.\nThe fourth table, \"postLinks,\" stores information about the links between posts, including the type of link and the posts it connects. Each row in this table represents a single link, and it includes columns for the link's ID, the date it was created, the post it is attached to, the related post it connects to, and the type of link.\nThe fifth table, \"posts,\" stores information about the questions and answers that users can ask and answer. Each row in this table represents a single post, and it includes columns for the post's ID, the type of post, the ID of the post that it answers, the date it was created, the score of the post, the view count, the body of the post, the ID of the user who created it, the date it was last active, the title of the post, the tags associated with the post, the number of answers, the number of comments, the number of favorites, the ID of the user who last edited it, the date it was last edited, the date it was community-owned, the ID of the parent post, the date it was closed, the display name of the user who created it, the display name of the user who last edited it, and the ID of the account that created it.\nThe sixth table, \"tags,\" stores information about the tags that users can apply to questions and answers. Each row in this table represents a single tag, and it includes columns for the tag's ID, the name of the tag, the number of times the tag has been used, the ID of the post that the tag is attached to, and the ID of the post that provides an example of the tag.\nThe seventh table, \"users,\" stores information about the users who contribute to the community. Each row in this table represents a single user, and it includes columns for the user's ID, the user's reputation, the date they joined, their display name, the date they last accessed the site, their website URL, their location, their about me section, their views, their up votes, their down votes, their account ID, their age, and their profile image URL.\nThe eighth and final table, \"votes,\" stores information about the votes that users can cast on questions and answers. Each row in this table represents a single vote, and it includes columns for the vote's ID, the post it is attached to, the type of vote, the date it was cast, the user who cast it, and the bounty amount.\nOverall, this schema provides a comprehensive and detailed view of the data that is stored in the Stack Overflow community, allowing for the creation of complex queries and reports that can be used to analyze and understand the behavior of the community.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a data management system for the Stats Stack Exchange network. The system captures and stores anonymized user-contributed content, facilitating the analysis and tracking of user interactions and contributions within the network.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to create a robust database that organizes and maintains structured data on user activities, posts, comments, and interactions. This supports data analysis and insights generation for community management and improvement.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Site Administrators: Manage the database and ensure data integrity.\n- Data Analysts: Use the data for insights and reporting.\n- Community Managers: Monitor user interactions and engagement.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. User Management: Maintain user profiles, including reputation, display name, and activity metrics.\n2. Post Management: Track posts, including creation dates, scores, view counts, and relationships with other posts.\n3. Comment Management: Record comments with associated metadata like scores, creation dates, and user information.\n4. Badge Management: Log badge awards to users, documenting achievement types and award dates.\n5. Vote Management: Capture votes on posts, detailing the type of vote and any associated bounty amounts.\n6. Tagging System: Organize content using tags; maintain information about tags and their associated posts.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a large volume of data with efficient query performance.\n- Data Integrity: Ensure consistency and accuracy of data, with cascade update and delete operations across related tables.\n- Anonymity: Maintain user anonymity while preserving engagement metrics.\n- Security: Protect sensitive data and limit access to authorized personnel only.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0130.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0130\nCREATE TABLE `badges` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_earned` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `badges_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `text` text NOT NULL,\n  `date_created` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `postHistory` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `revision_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `revision_guid` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_created` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `revision_text` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `postHistory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `postHistory_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `postLinks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `date_created` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `related_post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `link_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `postLinks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `postLinks_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`related_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `posts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_post_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_created` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `view_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date_last_active` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `answer_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `comment_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `favorite_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `last_edited_user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_last_edited` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_community_owned` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_closed` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_edited_display_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`last_edited_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `example_post_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`example_post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `reputation` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `date_joined` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_last_access` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `about_me` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `views` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `up_votes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `down_votes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `date_cast` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bounty_amount` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
